  "label": "Crematorium",
  "description": "A facility designed for the incineration of human remains. In the context of the Holocaust, crematoria were part of Nazi death camps and were used to dispose of the bodies of victims on a massive scale. The image shows a crematorium oven, which is a key piece of infrastructure in the genocide. Knowledge of its function and historical context is necessary to understand the scene.",
